                "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent works on an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, then gives a human admin an approve, reject, or request-info recommendation with its reasons. It auto-approves only when the evidence is verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve one.\n\nIt is currently in offline evals (31 cases). With Claude Haiku 5.5, which was chosen for deployment, accuracy was 86% and 1% of fraud was approved, compared with 71% accuracy and 8% fraud approved for the local 9B model. A review costs about $0.002."
